@page "/ai/scenarios/usage"
@inherits AppComponentBase

<PageOutlet Url="ai/scenarios/usage"
            Title="AI models, tokens and cost"
            Keywords="LLM model picker, token usage, AI cost tracking, context window meter, BitAiModelSelector, BitAiContextMeter, BitAiTokenUsageView"
            Description="A model picker in the composer of a bit BlazorUI AI chat, and real accounting under each answer: tokens, cost, throughput, and how much of the context window is used." />

<DocsArticle Eyebrow="AI scenarios"
             Title="Models and usage"
             Lead="A model picker in the composer, and real accounting under each answer: tokens, cost, throughput, and context used."
             GitHubUrl="AI/Scenarios/Usage/AiUsageScenarioPage.razor">

    <Badges>
        <BitTag Size="BitSize.Small" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Color="BitColor.SecondaryForeground" Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI" />
        <BitTag Size="BitSize.Small" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Color="BitColor.SecondaryForeground" Text="Scripted transport" />
    </Badges>

    <ChildContent>
        <DocSection Id="demo" Title="Live demo"
                    Description="Pick a model and ask something: the readout under the answer is priced with that model's rates.">
            <DemoExample Title="A model picker and a meter" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" CodeFiles="@example1CodeFiles" Id="example1">
                <AiScenarioFrame AsideLabel="Selected model">
                    <Aside>
                        <BitText Element="h4" Typography="BitTypography.Subtitle2">Selected model</BitText>
                        @if (_model is { } model)
                        {
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>@model.Name</strong></li>
                                <li>Context: @(model.ContextWindow?.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)) tokens</li>
                                <li>Input: @($"{model.InputPricePerMillion:0.##}") @model.Currency per million</li>
                                <li>Output: @($"{model.OutputPricePerMillion:0.##}") @model.Currency per million</li>
                                <li>Tools: @(model.Supports(BitAiModelCapabilities.Tools) ? "yes" : "no")</li>
                                <li>Vision: @(model.Supports(BitAiModelCapabilities.Vision) ? "yes" : "no")</li>
                            </ul>
                        }
                    </Aside>
                    <ChildContent>
                        <BitAiChat Session="_session"
                                   UiOptions="_options"
                                   EmptyTitle="Pick a model and ask something"
                                   Suggestions="_suggestions">
                            <ComposerPrefixTemplate>
                                <BitAiModelSelector @bind-ModelId="_modelId"
                                                    OnModelSelected="OnModelSelected"
                                                    Disabled="@(_session?.IsGenerating ?? false)" />
                            </ComposerPrefixTemplate>
                            <ComposerHintTemplate>
                                @* The window of the model picked now, rather than of the one the last reply ran on, which
                                   the conversation reports - a Model is only the fallback for a conversation that does not. *@
                                <BitAiContextMeter Conversation="_session?.Conversation" Window="_model?.ContextWindow" />
                            </ComposerHintTemplate>
                        </BitAiChat>
                    </ChildContent>
                </AiScenarioFrame>
            </DemoExample>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="how-it-works" Title="How it works">
            <p>
                The models come from the catalog registered with <code>ai.AddModels(models, providers, defaultModelId)</code>,
                which the selector reads (<code>IBitAiModelCatalog</code>), grouped by family or provider. Picking another one
                moves the conversation onto a new session for that model; the old session only has to stop.
            </p>
            <p>
                The choice reaches the transport in the session's <code>RequestOptions</code>, a
                <code>BitAiRequestOptions</code> sent with every request (<code>BitAiRequest.Options</code>): here its
                <code>ModelId</code> and <code>Temperature</code>. It also carries <code>ProviderId</code>,
                <code>TopP</code>, <code>MaxOutputTokens</code>, <code>StopSequences</code>, <code>Seed</code>,
                <code>SystemPrompt</code>, the <code>ToolChoice</code> (<BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/tools">Tool calling</BitLink>),
                the <code>ResponseFormat</code> (<BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/structured">Structured output</BitLink>) and an
                <code>Extra</code> dictionary for provider settings with no field of their own. Every one is optional, and a
                transport ignores what its provider cannot express. A session's <code>Options</code> can also be replaced
                between turns, when the transport itself stays the same.
            </p>
            <p>
                The transport reports back what it used: a <code>BitAiMetadataEvent</code> with the model, the provider, the
                context window and the temperature, merged into the reply's metadata, and a
                <code>BitAiUsageUpdatedEvent</code> with the input, output and cached tokens and the cost. Usage is cumulative
                within one stream - a later report replaces an earlier one, so a provider's running totals can be forwarded
                as they come - and the streams of one turn add up, one per tool round trip.
            </p>
            <p>
                Every field of the accounting is optional, because providers report different subsets of it. The components do
                the arithmetic they can: throughput from the output tokens over the streaming window, cost from the rates in
                the model catalog (<code>BitAiModel.EstimateCost</code>), and the share of the context window the conversation
                uses from the window the transport or the model reports. <code>ShowUsage</code>, <code>ShowModelName</code>
                and <code>ShowTimestamps</code> of <code>BitAiUiOptions</code> decide what a message shows.
            </p>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="components" Title="Components used">
            <ul>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/modelselector"><code>BitAiModelSelector</code></BitLink> - the picker, in the composer's prefix.</li>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/contextmeter"><code>BitAiContextMeter</code></BitLink> - the context used, in the composer's hint.</li>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/tokenusageview"><code>BitAiTokenUsageView</code></BitLink> - the tokens, cost and speed of each answer.</li>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/messageactions"><code>BitAiMessageActions</code></BitLink> - the row under an answer that carries the model, the usage and the time.</li>
            </ul>
        </DocSection>
    </ChildContent>

    <FooterTemplate>
        <DocPager Pages="AiScenarioNav.Items" AriaLabel="AI scenarios" />
    </FooterTemplate>
</DocsArticle>
